{
  "description": "Restore the Sprites shapes the published spec loses (regressed when #849 moved off the hand-written spec; observed by alchemy's live Sprite tests, which pass against these shapes). POST /sprites/{name}/exec answers with stdout/stderr/exit frames that SpritesProtocol decodes to { exit_code, stdout, stderr }, but the spec documents no body. Its `cmd` and `env` query parameters repeat (the spec says so in prose) but are typed as single strings. POST /sprites/{name}/checkpoint and .../restore stream NDJSON progress events, which the spec's oneOf converts to Unit. POST /sprites accepts `labels` (echoed on SpriteResponse.labels) and answers 409 for a name already in use. PUT .../services/{service_name} accepts a service without `args` or `needs`.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.flyio.sprites#ExecResult",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {
          "exit_code": { "target": "smithy.api#Integer" },
          "stdout": { "target": "smithy.api#String" },
          "stderr": { "target": "smithy.api#String" }
        },
        "traits": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.flyio.sprites#SpriteEnvExecuteCommand/output",
      "value": { "target": "com.flyio.sprites#ExecResult" }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
